venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.vscode/

# Derived caches and provider snapshots: rebuildable from data/raw/, so they
# stay out of git. Everything the replay proof needs is tracked below.
data/*.parquet
data/*_fundamentals_*.json
data/decision_audit.jsonl
data/paper_orders.jsonl

# The event-memory store. Its INFERRED memories are derived: the backfill
# rebuilds them deterministically from data/raw/ via
# `python scripts/build_event_memory.py --mode backfill --years 15`, so
# shipping ~3k generated rows would be committing a cache.
#
# NOTE for whoever turns the forward builder on: OBSERVED memories are NOT
# rebuildable, because the news window that produced them closes after
# NEWS_LOOKBACK_DAYS (7) and the articles are gone. Once real observed
# memories start accruing, this store stops being a cache and needs either a
# tracked observed-only file or a backup that is not git.
data/event_memory.jsonl

# Collection run artefacts. The report is an operational log of WHEN the
# collector ran, not evidence for any score, and collect.log is raw stdout.
# The coverage gate reads the report locally; committing it would mean every
# machine's schedule history colliding in one file.
data/collection_report.jsonl
data/collect.log

# The forecast ledger and its rotation cursor. The ledger is a local record of
# what THIS machine forecast and how those forecasts scored; committing it
# would mean every machine's scoreboard colliding in one file, and it grows
# ~24 MB/year at full portfolio coverage. It is rebuildable in the sense that
# re-running scripts/run_forecasts.py re-derives the same rows from the same
# memories — but the SCOREBOARD it accumulates is this machine's history.
data/forecast_ledger.jsonl
data/collect_cursor.json

# The NEWS ledger is the one W6 exception, and it is deliberate.
#
# MEASURED: news writes ~208 KB per ticker per day, so the 77-ticker universe
# produces ~15.7 MB/day, ~345 MB/month, ~3.9 GB/year. Git never forgets, so
# committing that is irreversible even if the files are deleted later, and
# GitHub soft-warns at 1 GB. The repo would be unusable within months.
#
# CONSEQUENCE, stated plainly: a fresh clone can still replay every PRICE-,
# FUNDAMENTALS- and MACRO-derived score from raw records, which is what the
# W6 acceptance proof covers. It CANNOT replay a news-derived sentiment or an
# OBSERVED event memory, because those raw articles live only on the machine
# that collected them. That machine needs a backup that is not git.
data/raw/newsapi_news/

# NOT ignored (tracked on purpose): the rest of data/raw/ is the W6
# append-only provenance ledger and data/feature_registry.jsonl is the M1
# registry. "delete derived cache -> rebuild from raw -> reproduce the same
# result" is only executable by a fresh clone if these travel with the repo.

# C2: the reproducibility gate's dataset cache. DERIVED — the build is
# deterministic (verified: identical dataset_hash across builds), so the cache is
# a speed-up and never an input. Committing it would ship a pickle of rebuildable
# data, and a stale one would make the gate measure the cache rather than the code.
data/.cache/
